  data:  # bbb1
    kind: work_item  # bbb1
    title: "undocumented additive in-degree confidence boost (cap +0.35, library_export) at entrypoints.py:1504-1507; spec documents only out-degree"  # bbb1
    status: todo_hard  # bbb1
    priority: 2  # bbb1
    parent:  # bbb1
    tags:  # bbb1
    - dogfood  # bbb1
    - dogfood_tranche_06  # bbb1
    isbefore: []  # bbb1
    duplicate_of: []  # bbb1
    not_duplicate_of: []  # bbb1
    pr_ref:  # bbb1
    description: "**Defect.** Entrypoint confidence carries an undocumented additive in-degree boost beyond the single boost the spec describes.\n\n**Evidence.** After base-tier detection, a post-detection pipeline applies an additive in-degree connectivity boost (cap +0.35, for library_export entrypoints) at entrypoints.py:1504-1507. The spec's adjustment section (§895) documents only an out-degree boost (\"+0.25 for entrypoints with many outgoing edges\"); the in-degree boost is in the producer but not in the spec (grep of §895 names only \"outgoing edges\").\n\n**Contract.** Every confidence adjustment the producer applies should be documented in the spec's confidence-adjustment section, or removed from the producer.\n\n**Consequence.** Library-export entrypoint confidence partly encodes in-degree (caller count) rather than detection reliability, and a consumer reverse-engineering how an entrypoint's confidence was computed cannot reconstruct the value from the documented adjustments."  # bbb1
    fields: {}  # bbb1
- op: discuss  # c295
  at: '2026-06-11T04:25:54Z'  # c295
  by: agent  # c295
